1. Project Overview
ASTROHEALTH is a health monitoring web application designed to monitor the health conditions of astronauts during space missions.
It provides a simple and user-friendly dashboard to display important health information such as heart rate, oxygen level, and body temperature.
The application helps identify abnormal health readings through alerts, making it easier for Mission Control to monitor astronaut health conditions.
Key Features

- Health monitoring dashboard.
- Display of heart rate, oxygen level, and body temperature.
- Alerts for abnormal health readings.
- Simple and user-friendly interface.
- Visual representation of health information.
- Easy-to-understand health status.

